// 1954
[uitutorial_combat_academy_session_6_part6]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,When you build up to 50% adrenaline, a Threshold ability should automatically be used.<br>Threshold abilities will use up 15% of your maximum adrenaline when activated.<br>Threshold abilities are much more powerful than basic abilities.
data=col10,1
data=col23,toplevel_v2_combat_bar:button_holder_6,-1
data=col23,toplevel_v2_combat_bar:button_holder_7,-1

// 1955
[uitutorial_combat_academy_session_6_part6_mobile]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,When you build up to 50% adrenaline, a Threshold ability should automatically be used.<br>Threshold abilities will use up 15% of your maximum adrenaline when activated.<br>Threshold abilities are much more powerful than basic abilities.
data=col10,1
data=col23,toplevel_v2_combat_bar_mobile_buttons:button_holder_5,-1
data=col23,toplevel_v2_combat_bar_mobile_buttons:button_holder_6,-1

// 1956
[uitutorial_combat_academy_session_6_part7]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,Fill your adrenaline bar to 100% then activate an ultimate ability.<br>Revolution uses your abilities from left to right, so you may need to click an Ultimate ability to queue it, or drag it in front of your Threshold abilities.<br>Ultimate abilities are the most powerful abilities, but use all your adrenaline.
data=col10,1
data=col23,toplevel_v2_combat_bar:button_holder_8,-1
data=col23,toplevel_v2_combat_bar:button_holder_9,-1

// 1957
[uitutorial_combat_academy_session_6_part7_mobile]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,Fill your adrenaline bar to 100% then activate an ultimate ability.<br>Revolution uses your abilities from left to right, so you may need to tap an Ultimate ability to queue it, or drag it in front of your Threshold abilities.<br>Ultimate abilities are the most powerful abilities, but use all your adrenaline.
data=col10,1
data=col23,toplevel_v2_combat_bar_mobile_buttons:button_holder_7,-1

// 1958
[uitutorial_combat_academy_session_6_part8]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,Use the food table to collect food for the upcoming fight.<br>Use the armour stands behind to gear up and restock ammunition for the upcoming fight.

// 1959
[uitutorial_combat_academy_session_6_challenge]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,Use basic abilities to build your adrenaline.<br>Use threshold abilities to wear your opponent down.<br>Use ultimate abilities to deal huge damage to your opponent.
data=col8,1
data=col10,1
data=col12,1

// 1960
[uitutorial_combat_academy_session_7_part1]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,Melee users like to get up close and personal to kill their foe.<br>Ranged users like to pick off their foe from a distance.<br>Magic users like to cast spells at their foe from a distance.
data=col10,1

// 1961
[uitutorial_combat_academy_session_7_part2]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,Try performing actions to see what you can and cannot do while stunned.

// 1962
[uitutorial_combat_academy_session_7_part2_next]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,Dummy text - Player should not see.

// 1963
[uitutorial_combat_academy_session_7_part2_2]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,While stunned, you cannot perform any actions, including eating and turning on prayers.
data=col13,1

// 1964
[uitutorial_combat_academy_session_7_part2_2_next]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,Dummy text - Player should not see.

// 1965
[uitutorial_combat_academy_session_7_part2_3]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,You can break out of a stun with the <col=FFCB05>Freedom</col> ability.<br>You can protect yourself from being stunned with the <col=FFCB05>Anticipation</col> ability.<br>You can find these in your <col=FFCB05>Defence Abilities</col> book.
data=col13,1
data=col17,"aif_attrib_defence_icons_1,1"
data=col18,"aif_attrib_defence_icons_1,0"
data=col23,toplevel_v2_combat_bar:button_highlight_1,-1

