// 2540
[uitutorial_skills_0]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,You have many skills you can train.<br>The more you practice a skill, the better it gets.<br><br>Higher skill levels unlock new activities: equipment to craft, locations to explore, quests to complete, and much more.
data=col6,stats_child:canvas
data=col7,-1
data=col8,3
data=col17,"staticons_high_res_clean,0"

// 2541
[uitutorial_skills_1]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,Perform actions associated with a skill to earn experience points (XP) in that skill.<br>Earn enough XP, and you'll gain a level in that skill.
data=col6,stats_child:canvas
data=col7,-1
data=col8,3
data=col17,"staticons_high_res_clean,0"
data=col18,"aif_money_xp_icons,0"
data=col19,"aif_level_up_text_language_gold,3"

// 2542
[uitutorial_skills_2]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,Most skills start at level 1, and you unlock all their benefits by leveling the skill to 99.<br>(Some skills have unlocks up to level 120.)
data=col6,stats_child:canvas
data=col7,-1
data=col8,3

// 2543
[uitutorial_skills_3]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,The bottom number next to a skill icon is your base level in that skill (un-modified by buffs or debuffs). It is used for most requirement checks.
data=col6,stats_child:canvas
data=col7,-1
data=col8,3
data=col23,stats_child:stat_base,2

// 2544
[uitutorial_skills_4]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,The top number is your modified skill level (temporarily boosted or drained by skill buffs and debuffs - such as potions or spells). It is used for most skill checks.
data=col6,stats_child:canvas
data=col7,-1
data=col8,3
data=col23,stats_child:stat,2

// 2545
[uitutorial_skills_5]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,Achieve 99 in all your skills to earn the coveted Max Cape!
