// 3216
[arch_research_infernalsource_star_lodge]
table=arch_research
data=col0,13
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_infernalsource
data=col3,Starry Eyed
data=col4,20
data=col6,This building upon which the Jolly Boar Inn was built appears to be a lodge of some sort.
data=col7,Paperwork found onsite suggests this place was named Star Lodge. Records show it was buried by the Forinthry explosion, and the Jolly Boar built atop it in a subsequent age.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_opulent_wine_goblet_damaged,1

// 3217
[arch_research_infernalsource_dungeon_of_disorder]
table=arch_research
data=col0,14
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_infernalsource
data=col3,The Dark Underbelly
data=col4,36
data=col6,A secret cult was in hiding beneath the lodge. This place is creepy.
data=col7,Symbology found in the dungeon matches that of a rumoured cult known as the Order of Dis, previously only thought to be a myth. It seems these followers of Zamorak hid in plain sight under the auspices of Saradomin and kept their presence secret for an age!
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_ritual_dagger_damaged,1

// 3218
[arch_research_infernalsource_vestibule_of_futility]
table=arch_research
data=col0,15
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_infernalsource
data=col3,Abandon All Hope
data=col4,29
data=col6,We're unsure where the portal has led, but we've made a significant discovery! Navigating this chaotic space is, however, proving tricky for our dig teams.
data=col7,Research places the Infernal Source directly beneath the Wilderness Crater! To think this place was here, abandoned, all this time. The research team have reported on a very vocal imp being found in this area and suggest you investigate...
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_dis_mask_imp_damaged,1

// 3219
[arch_research_infernalsource_harrowing]
table=arch_research
data=col0,16
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_infernalsource
data=col3,Deeper and Down
data=col4,68
data=col6,As the team delves deeper into the Infernal Source, the landscape is becoming more alien and unwelcoming, for example a sculpture made from hellhound skulls.
data=col7,That demonic remains even exist in this space in fossilised form suggests this space may cross over with infernal space in some way. One of the hellhound skulls had a dog collar placed around its neck, sporting the name 'Duke'.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_spiked_dog_collar_damaged,1

// 3220
[arch_research_infernalsource_dagon_overlook]
table=arch_research
data=col0,17
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_infernalsource
data=col3,Who Dis?
data=col4,68
data=col6,The source of the screaming seems to be a demonic entity trapped at the bottom of this space. None of our archaeologists dare to venture that far down.
data=col7,What we can see from the level above is that the demon below is trapped somehow. It is also surrounded by a twelve-headed circular statue, but we are not quite sure what any of it means at this point. We need to get closer, but the portal is too chaotic - we need to figure out how to make it work.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_chaos_star_damaged,1

// 3221
[arch_research_infernalsource_hydra_gate]
table=arch_research
data=col0,18
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_infernalsource
data=col3,Hell Mouths
data=col4,98
data=col6,Upon closer inspection, the twelve-headed circular statue matches descriptions of an ages-old entity, an incredibly large specimen of a hydra.
data=col7,Wow! What a find! Researchers have found the hydra gate was at one point a living creature! The petrified remains appear to match descriptions of an ancient deity named Loarnab. It still hums with a small amount of residual energy.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_hellfire_katar_damaged,1

