// 3250
[arch_kharidet_opening_cutscene]
table=image_sequence
data=col0,10
data=col1,30
data=col3,arch_cutscene_kharidet_01,The Zarosian Empire's very existence was once the greatest of archaeological<br>mysteries for us to uncover, and we achieved that here at Senntisten.,arch_opening_cutscene_kharidet_01,600,true,false,true,true
data=col3,arch_cutscene_kharidet_01,And although the empire was supposedly sprawling, it was so utterly destroyed<br>that finding a near intact fort buried beneath the sands is cause for celebration!,arch_opening_cutscene_kharidet_02,600,false,true,true,true
data=col3,arch_cutscene_kharidet_02a,The monolith has a strong connection with something buried deep beneath this<br>fort, however. Was the monolith itself Zarosian? No, surely not; it's beyond ancient.,arch_opening_cutscene_kharidet_03,750,true,false,true,true
data=col3,arch_cutscene_kharidet_02a,There is only one way to find out what the connection is.<br>We must dig deep at Kharid-et and discover what lies beneath...,arch_opening_cutscene_kharidet_04,600,false,true,true,true

// 3251
[arch_kharidet_closing_cutscene]
table=image_sequence
data=col0,11
data=col1,30
data=col3,arch_cutscene_kharidet_01,Kharid-et was truly forsaken. Though it fell right at the beginning of the Third Age,<br>it has remained untouched for millenia.,arch_closing_cutscene_kharidet_01,500,true,false,true,true
data=col3,arch_cutscene_kharidet_01,The place is filled with the ghosts of its past.<br>It's a wonder none of the archaeologists have encountered them so far.,arch_closing_cutscene_kharidet_02,450,false,true,true,true
data=col3,arch_cutscene_kharidet_02b,It is clear to us now why the monolith wished for us to dig here.<br>The magical readings are off the charts!,arch_closing_cutscene_kharidet_03,450,true,false,true,true
data=col3,arch_cutscene_kharidet_02b,I feel we have only scratched the surface of what<br>ancient magical power sits beneath here, buried in the shadows...,arch_closing_cutscene_kharidet_04,550,false,true,true,true

