// 3282
[arch_research_kharidet_breached_wall]
table=arch_research
data=col0,19
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_kharidet
data=col3,Demon Door
data=col4,12
data=col6,The wall we are using to enter Kharid-et was seemingly breached from the outside long ago.
data=col7,Research suggests Kharid-et was under siege by an army of demons loyal to Zamorak, very early on in the Third Age. The protective shield that sometimes activates here must have been breached.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_legionary_gladius_damaged,1
data=col15,arch_kharidet_pylon_battery,10

// 3283
[arch_research_kharidet_castra]
table=arch_research
data=col0,20
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_kharidet
data=col3,Proving Grounds
data=col4,17
data=col6,The castra, which roughly translates to 'camp', was primarily where the rank and file soldiers resided in the fort.
data=col7,This area of Kharid-et was mostly used as a training ground, as well as housing for legionaries, though some buildings appear to have been reserved for imperial officers.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_zarosian_training_dummy_damaged,1

// 3284
[arch_research_kharidet_carcerem]
table=arch_research
data=col0,21
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_kharidet
data=col3,Cell, a Door
data=col4,47
data=col6,The carcerem, which translates to 'prison', was an area of the fort used to temporarily hold lawbreakers.
data=col7,The team suggest that the various magical Legatus and Pontifex barriers could be passed through if you hold or wear the correct artefact...but they aren't sure which artefacts.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_legatus_pendant_damaged,1

// 3285
[arch_research_kharidet_sanctum]
table=arch_research
data=col0,22
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_kharidet
data=col3,Requiescat in Pace
data=col4,86
data=col6,The sanctum, or chapel, is primarily where members of the Zarosian Church went for worship.
data=col7,This particular sanctum appears to have paid fealty to a demon named Orcus - one of the empire's chthonian dukes, according to Dr Nabanik - who was supposedly known for its necromantic ability. Orcus's inverted pentagram symbology is abundant.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_necromantic_focus_damaged,1

// 3286
[arch_research_kharidet_culinarum]
table=arch_research
data=col0,23
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_kharidet
data=col3,Where There's Smoke...
data=col4,100
data=col6,The culinarum, or kitchens, are pretty standard fare for a fort of this size.
data=col7,There's not a huge deal of interest to be found in the kitchens, save for a strange device on one of the walls there. This kitchen could have served food to an entire legion - over a thousand troops and support staff!
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_spell_smoke_cloud_damaged,1

// 3287
[arch_research_kharidet_praetorium]
table=arch_research
data=col0,24
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_kharidet
data=col3,Shadow Play
data=col4,107
data=col6,How unusual - an entire building hidden away in an overlapping realm!
data=col7,The praetorium has somehow been shifted into the Shadow Realm in order to hide its existence! It took the shield pylon effect and another shadow delving ability to even see the war table, which suggests multiple levels of shadow. Perhaps there is something else even deeper?
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_spell_animate_dead_damaged,1

// 3288
[arch_research_kharidet_vault_of_shadows]
table=arch_research
data=col0,25
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_kharidet
data=col3,Lockdown
data=col4,58
data=col6,There is a hidden vault beneath Kharid-et! What wonders might it hold?
data=col7,Research suggests other, smaller vaults may still be hidden here, but the one we've discovered was clearly of great importance to be hidden how it was. The team wonders what it might contain within...
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_pontifex_signet_ring_damaged,1

// 3289
[arch_restoration_kharidet_access_seal]
table=arch_restoration
data=col0,151
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_kharidet_access_seal
data=col3,This seal contains innate magic allowing wielders to pass through Kharid-et's protective barrier. It would have been used by the fort's soldiers and scouting parties to quickly and easily return into the safety of the fort.
data=col4,12
data=col5,arch_restoration_kharidet_access_seal_damaged
data=col6,arch_kharidet_access_seal
data=col7,0
data=col8,0

