// 3355
[arch_warforge_opening_cutscene]
table=image_sequence
data=col0,18
data=col1,30
data=col3,arch_cutscene_warforge_01,The monolith shared what it could about the Warforge,<br>but it's as you would expect from a Bandosian construction.,arch_opening_cutscene_warforge_01,400,true,false,true,true
data=col3,arch_cutscene_warforge_01,Bandos's mercenary armies are quite well documented in comparison to<br>other Third Age events, after all, and they had to be trained somewhere.,arch_opening_cutscene_warforge_02,500,false,true,true,true
data=col3,arch_cutscene_warforge_02a,What strikes me most, however, is that the few artefacts discovered so far<br>are not consistent with other Bandosian creations.,arch_opening_cutscene_warforge_03,450,true,false,true,true
data=col3,arch_cutscene_warforge_02a,Who or what created the armaments for Bandos's mercenaries,<br>and why is this secret so well buried?,arch_opening_cutscene_warforge_04,450,false,true,true,true

// 3356
[arch_warforge_closing_cutscene]
table=image_sequence
data=col0,19
data=col1,30
data=col3,arch_cutscene_warforge_01,Bandos's capriciousness and cruelty knew no bounds.<br>Prior to his eviction, he buried his goblin charges beneath the dirt.,arch_closing_cutscene_warforge_01,500,true,false,true,true
data=col3,arch_cutscene_warforge_01,Left them to splinter and fight, trapped in darkness - the Forge Wars - and to<br>devolve into beings bent only on fighting for survival.,arch_closing_cutscene_warforge_02,600,false,true,true,true
data=col3,arch_cutscene_warforge_02b,The abducted Imcando dwarf, Thalmund, once the flaming heart<br>of the Warforge, was their only saviour.,arch_closing_cutscene_warforge_03,450,true,false,true,true
data=col3,arch_cutscene_warforge_02b,All goblins revered him for his fine weaponsmithing, and<br>so was he able to eventually dig an escape tunnel and lead them back to the surface.,arch_closing_cutscene_warforge_04,600,false,true,true,true

