// 4464
[arch_research_senntisten_cathedral]
table=arch_research
data=col0,57
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_senntisten
data=col3,The Hidden Chamber
data=col4,60
data=col6,There is a hidden part of the Cathedral connected to the statues and the Shadow Realm. If we can uncover the secret, imagine what we could discover.
data=col7,We uncovered what appears to be a secret laboratory dedicated to studying the Monolith. What was Zaros doing here?
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_funerary_urn_of_shadow_damaged,1

// 4465
[arch_research_senntisten_marketplace]
table=arch_research
data=col0,58
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_senntisten
data=col3,Prime Real Estate
data=col4,63
data=col6,The markets of Senntisten are a mystery to us. Was their trade system as carefully organised as their political structure?
data=col7,The markets of Senntisten were carefully licensed, with various tiers of status that granted access to more lucrative contracts and desirable tax breaks.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_funerary_urn_of_ice_damaged,1

// 4466
[arch_research_senntisten_bridge]
table=arch_research
data=col0,59
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_senntisten
data=col3,Crossing that Bridge
data=col4,67
data=col6,North of the plaza lies the crumbling ruins of a magnificent bridge. With some work, we could make it more accessible.
data=col7,With some carefully placed scaffolding, we can now access the magnificent view of the bridge over the Senntisten waterways.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_funerary_urn_of_smoke_damaged,1

// 4467
[arch_research_senntisten_colosseum]
table=arch_research
data=col0,60
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_senntisten
data=col3,Are You Not Entertained?
data=col4,66
data=col6,The Colosseum was once the central entertainment hub of the Empire. What games did they play here?
data=col7,The Colosseum was home to brutal gladiatorial battles and magnificent demon-drawn chariot races. It would have been a crowded building in its heyday.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_restoration_funerary_urn_of_blood_damaged,1

// 4468
[arch_research_senntisten_puzzle_box]
table=arch_research
data=col0,61
data=col1,2
data=col2,arch_site_senntisten
data=col3,Complete the Pattern, Solve the Puzzle
data=col4,63
data=col6,This ancient puzzle box is still surprisingly well preserved. It sounds as if there is something inside it.
data=col7,It took some time to unlock the secrets of the puzzle box. That is, the researchers smashed it against a rock in a fit of frustration. Inside, there was a well-preserved letter.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,arch_senntisten_lore_empty_children_page04,1

