// 5354
[uitutorial_helpbutton_worldmap_0]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,The World Map shows all the main features of the game world.<br><br>To explore the map, simply move the mouse while holding down the <col=FFcb05>left mouse button</col>. To zoom in and out, use the <col=FFcb05>mouse wheel</col>.

// 5355
[uitutorial_helpbutton_worldmap_0_mobile]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,The World Map shows all the main features of the game world.<br><br><col=FFcb05>Drag your finger</col> to move the map. <col=FFcb05>Pinch your fingers</col> to zoom in and out.

// 5356
[uitutorial_helpbutton_worldmap_1]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,The key explains what the different map icons mean.<br><br>To control the amount of information shown on the map, use the checkboxes to turn the icons on and off.
data=col6,worldmap_v2_ui:key_group
data=col7,-1
data=col8,4
data=col17,rs3_icon_worldmap_bank

// 5357
[uitutorial_helpbutton_worldmap_2]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,The World Map opens centred on your current map position.<br><br>If you want to look at a different map, such as a dungeon interior, or the RuneScape Surface when you're underground, you can choose the map here.
data=col6,worldmap_v2_ui:map_menu_layer
data=col7,-1
data=col8,1

// 5358
[uitutorial_helpbutton_worldmap_3]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,If you know the name of the place you're looking for, you can type it into this search box to look for a map label.
data=col6,worldmap_v2_ui:findbox
data=col7,-1
data=col8,1

// 5359
[uitutorial_helpbutton_worldmap_4]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,You can double-click the map to set a map marker.<br><br>You can clear your map marker from the Legend or by right-clicking your map marker.
data=col17,"rs3_icon_worldmap_locators,3"

// 5360
[uitutorial_helpbutton_worldmap_4_mobile]
table=uitutorial_step
data=col3,You can double-tap the map to set a map marker.<br><br>You can clear your map marker from the Legend or by holding over your map marker.
data=col17,"rs3_icon_worldmap_locators,3"

